# a part of the day fused with TODAY, as English "tonight" is: "i" before a
# bare part-of-day noun names today's band.  "i natt" is "tonight" or "last
# night" (https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/i_natt), and "i ettermiddag tar jeg
# fri" is this afternoon (Bokmålsordboka, ettermiddag,
# https://ordbokene.no/bm/13299); "i formiddag" and "i kveld" follow the
# same pattern.
i formiddag
i ettermiddag
i kveld
i natt
